    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAINTED BY J. P. BUTTERWORTH\nonald Mo Kay Org. Builder of the Leviathon\nCLIPPER SUN «GREAT REPUBLIC\"\nLITH. BY N. CURRIER",
      "THE PRESIDENT\nBOiSSONS\nSherry Dubonnet Campari Vermouth See\nManhattan Martini Daiquie\nBloody Mary\nScrewdriver\nWhiskey Sour\nTom Collins\nValka Collins\nScotch Bourbon Caradian\nGin Vodka Rum\nBeer\nNOTRE SELECTiON DES GRANDS ViNS\nOUR SELECTION OF VINTAGE WINES\nVins de Bourgogne Têre de Cuvée Vins de Bordeaux Grand Crâ classe\nGREAT WINES OF BURGUNDY\nGREAT WINES OF BORDEAUX\nChampagne Brue Millésimé- Cuvée spéciale pour Pan American\nCHAMPAGNE SPECIALLY SELECTED FOR PAN\nAMERICAN\nCointreau Drambuie Bénédictine\nCème do Methe Cognac VP Boticine et Brand\nSPECIAL\nDiNER\nHORS D'OFUVRE\nCocktail de Truits de Mer\nSEAFOOD COCKTAIL\nENTREES\nFilet Mignon Metropolis\nFILET MIGNON WITH SHERRY CREAM SAUCE\nCurry de Roulet Madras\nURRIED CHICKEN MADRA\nLegumes de Jardin, au baurre\nRig Pilaff\nBUTTERED GARDEN VEGETABLES\nPILAFF RICE\nDESSERTS\nTromage\nCHEESE AND CRACKERS\nPatisserie\nFRENCH PASTRY\nDemi-Tasse\nCafé Americain\nDEMITASSE\nAMERICAN COFFEE\nThe Orange Phoe\nORANGE PEKOE TEA\nPAN AMERiCAN CUiSiNE BY MAXiM'S DE. PARiS\n871. •*.•",
      "Built by Donald McKay and launched in 1853 in East Boston, the clipper ship\n\"Great Republic\"\nwas the summit of achievement in the world of sailing ships.\nShe was, from the standpoint of size, appearance and cost... the King of Clippers.\nThe \"Great Republic\"\nwas considered\nicent craft ever produced by any nation or age.\nthe largest, sharpest and most magnif\nBefore she had barely tasted\nsalt water, fire broke out in her New\nYork wharf, and within minutes the \"Great\nRepublic\" was a network of flames. She was later rebuilt but with her tonnage,\nsail plan and spars reduced.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers® of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the\nlanes of commerce to all far places of the world. Pan Am's Clipper fleet of the\n20th Century\nconsists\nthe\nfinest commercial aircraft\never developed...\nClippers that helped Pan Am establish an unparalleled record for safety, speed\nand service.\nThis is a faithful reproduction of an\nauthentic Currier \u0026 Ives lithograph, repro-\nduced through the courtesy of the Mariners\nMuseum, Newport News,\nVirginia.\n2016.117.144 LITHO U.S. A."
    ],
